Render the groupbar gradient textures one pixel wide

The four groupbar gradient textures (active, inactive, locked active,
locked inactive) were rendered at the full size of the focused monitor and
kept for the life of the compositor, even when no group exists. The gradient
only varies along y, and the texture is stretched over each bar with linear
filtering and clamp-to-edge, so a single column gives the same pixels.

At 3024x1964 this frees 4 x 22.7 MiB of GPU memory; at 3840x2160 it is
4 x 31.6 MiB.

diff --git a/src/render/decorations/CHyprGroupBarDecoration.cpp b/src/render/decorations/CHyprGroupBarDecoration.cpp
index 5a40e98cd..96278949c 100644
--- a/src/render/decorations/CHyprGroupBarDecoration.cpp
+++ b/src/render/decorations/CHyprGroupBarDecoration.cpp
@@ -324,7 +324,10 @@ static SP<ITexture> renderGradient(Config::CGradientValueData* grad) {
     if (!Desktop::focusState()->monitor())
         return nullptr;
 
-    const Vector2D& bufferSize = Desktop::focusState()->monitor()->m_transformedSize;
+    // The gradient only varies vertically and the texture is stretched over each bar with
+    // linear filtering and clamp-to-edge, so a single column samples exactly like a full-width
+    // image. A monitor-wide image costs width * height * 4 bytes per texture (four of them).
+    const Vector2D bufferSize = {1.0, Desktop::focusState()->monitor()->m_transformedSize.y};
 
     const auto      CAIROSURFACE = cairo_image_surface_create(CAIRO_FORMAT_ARGB32, bufferSize.x, bufferSize.y);
     const auto      CAIRO        = cairo_create(CAIROSURFACE);
